{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","title":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.md","line":411,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula]]","[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex","label":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","line":872,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[hat-tensor formula for Weitzenb\\\"ock curvature]\n  \\label{lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0368}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued, def:pet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator, lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula}\n  \\dcref{ch9:9.4.9}\n  For any two $(0,k)$-tensors $T$ and $S$, contraction of their hat tensors\n  gives\n  \\[\n    g(\\operatorname{Ric}(T),S)=g(\\mathfrak R(\\hat T),\\hat S).\n  \\]\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula}\n  \\sketch\n  In orthonormal bases \\(e_I\\) and \\(\\Xi_\\sigma\\), use\n  \\cref{lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula} and the definition in\n  \\cref{def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued} to write\n  \\[\n    g(\\operatorname{Ric}(T),S)\n      =\\sum_{\\sigma,I}g(\\Xi_\\sigma,\\hat T(e_I))\n        g(R(\\Xi_\\sigma),\\hat S(e_I)).\n  \\]\n  Resumming the \\(\\Xi_\\sigma\\)-components is precisely\n  \\(g(\\mathfrak R(\\hat T),\\hat S)\\).\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[hat-tensor formula for Weitzenböck curvature] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368392d7269632d6375727661747572652d6f70657261746f722d6861742d666f726d756c61\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0368</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23def%3Apet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued\">↗ def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23def%3Apet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator\">↗ def:pet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23lem%3Apet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula\">↗ lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula</a> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch9:9.4.9</span></span>For any two <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(0,k)$\">$(0,k)$</span>-tensors <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T$\">$T$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$S$\">$S$</span>, contraction of their hat tensors gives <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  g(\\operatorname {Ric}(T),S)=g(\\mathfrak R(\\hat T),\\hat S).  \\]\">\\[  g(\\operatorname {Ric}(T),S)=g(\\mathfrak R(\\hat T),\\hat S).  \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23lem%3Apet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula\">↗ lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula</a> \\sketch In orthonormal bases <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$e_I$\">$e_I$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Xi _\\sigma $\">$\\Xi _\\sigma $</span>, use <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23lem%3Apet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7065742d6368392d7269632d6375727661747572652d6f70657261746f722d666f726d756c61\">subsection 3.3</a> and the definition in <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23def%3Apet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued\" data-tex-node=\"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368392d74656e736f722d6c616d626461322d76616c756564\">subsection 4.5</a> to write </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  g(\\operatorname {Ric}(T),S) =\\sum _{\\sigma ,I}g(\\Xi _\\sigma ,\\hat T(e_I)) g(R(\\Xi _\\sigma ),\\hat S(e_I)).  \\]\">\\[  g(\\operatorname {Ric}(T),S) =\\sum _{\\sigma ,I}g(\\Xi _\\sigma ,\\hat T(e_I)) g(R(\\Xi _\\sigma ),\\hat S(e_I)).  \\]</span></p><p> Resumming the <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Xi _\\sigma $\">$\\Xi _\\sigma $</span>-components is precisely <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g(\\mathfrak R(\\hat T),\\hat S)$\">$g(\\mathfrak R(\\hat T),\\hat S)$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued","next":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#prop:pet-ch9-1form-hat-ricci","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued","title":"def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued","label":"def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator","title":"def:pet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator","label":"def:pet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula","title":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula","label":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","title":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","label":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","title":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","label":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#prop:pet-ch9-1form-hat-ricci","title":"prop:pet-ch9-1form-hat-ricci","label":"prop:pet-ch9-1form-hat-ricci"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","title":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[hat-tensor formula for Weitzenb\\\"ock curvature]\n  \\label{lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0368}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued, def:pet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator, lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula}\n  \\dcref{ch9:9.4.9}\n  For any two $(0,k)$-tensors $T$ and $S$, contraction of their hat tensors\n  gives\n  \\[\n    g(\\operatorname{Ric}(T),S)=g(\\mathfrak R(\\hat T),\\hat S).\n  \\]\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n  \\uses{lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-hat-formula}\n  \\sketch\n  In orthonormal bases \\(e_I\\) and \\(\\Xi_\\sigma\\), use\n  \\cref{lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula} and the definition in\n  \\cref{def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued} to write\n  \\[\n    g(\\operatorname{Ric}(T),S)\n      =\\sum_{\\sigma,I}g(\\Xi_\\sigma,\\hat T(e_I))\n        g(R(\\Xi_\\sigma),\\hat S(e_I)).\n  \\]\n  Resumming the \\(\\Xi_\\sigma\\)-components is precisely\n  \\(g(\\mathfrak R(\\hat T),\\hat S)\\).\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued","title":"def:pet-ch9-tensor-lambda2-valued","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator","title":"def:pet-ch9-weitzenbock-curvature-operator","description":""},{"node":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula","title":"lem:pet-ch9-ric-curvature-operator-formula","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}